### ============================================================
### Job Application Tracker — Demo Walkthrough
### ============================================================
###
### Demonstrates the full feature set of the API in a realistic
### job-search scenario. Run requests top to bottom against a
### clean database.
###
### Setup:
###   docker compose down -v
###   docker compose up -d
###   mvn spring-boot:run
###
### Then run each request in order using the IntelliJ HTTP client.
### The JWT captured from step 1 is reused automatically in all
### subsequent requests via the {{jwt_token}} variable.
### ============================================================


### ============================================================
### STEP 1 — Register a new user and capture the JWT
### ============================================================

POST http://localhost:8080/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "riley",
  "password": "demo1234"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("jwt_token", response.body.token);
%}


### ============================================================
### STEP 2 — Set up companies
### Two companies being actively targeted in the job search
### ============================================================

### Create company 1: Google
POST http://localhost:8080/api/companies
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt_token}}

{
  "name": "Google",
  "location": "Seattle, WA",
  "website": "google.com",
  "industry": "Technology"
}

###

### Create company 2: Microsoft
POST http://localhost:8080/api/companies
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt_token}}

{
  "name": "Microsoft",
  "location": "Redmond, WA",
  "website": "microsoft.com",
  "industry": "Technology"
}

###

### Verify both companies exist
GET http://localhost:8080/api/companies
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt_token}}


### ============================================================
### STEP 3 — Add contacts at each company
### Contacts represent recruiters/hiring managers and can be
### optionally linked to an application
### ============================================================

### Create contact at Google: engineering manager
POST http://localhost:8080/api/contacts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt_token}}

{
  "name": "John Smith",
  "title": "Engineering Manager",
  "email": "john.smith@google.com",
  "phoneNumber": "425-555-1234",
  "companyId": 1
}

###

### Create contact at Microsoft: recruiter
POST http://localhost:8080/api/contacts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt_token}}

{
  "name": "Jane Doe",
  "title": "Senior Recruiter",
  "email": "jane.doe@microsoft.com",
  "phoneNumber": "425-555-5678",
  "companyId": 2
}

###

### Filter contacts by company — confirm John is under Google (id: 1)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/contacts/search?companyId=1
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt_token}}


### ============================================================
### STEP 4 — Add job listings
### Each listing belongs to a company and can have one application
### ============================================================

### Google listing 1: Backend Developer (OPEN)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/job-listings
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt_token}}

{
  "title": "Backend Developer",
  "description": "Java backend role focused on Spring Boot microservices",
  "salaryMin": 90000,
  "salaryMax": 120000,
  "listingStatus": "OPEN",
  "datePosted": "2026-02-01",
  "companyId": 1
}

###

### Google listing 2: Senior Engineer (OPEN)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/job-listings
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt_token}}

{
  "title": "Senior Engineer",
  "description": "Senior Java role with team lead responsibilities",
  "salaryMin": 130000,
  "salaryMax": 160000,
  "listingStatus": "OPEN",
  "datePosted": "2026-01-15",
  "companyId": 1
}

###

### Microsoft listing: Java Developer (OPEN)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/job-listings
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt_token}}

{
  "title": "Java Developer",
  "description": "Java developer role on the Azure platform team",
  "salaryMin": 95000,
  "salaryMax": 125000,
  "listingStatus": "OPEN",
  "datePosted": "2026-01-20",
  "companyId": 2
}

###

### Filter listings by company — all Google listings (companyId: 1)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/job-listings/search?companyId=1
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt_token}}

###

### Filter listings by status — all OPEN listings across companies
GET http://localhost:8080/api/job-listings/search?listingStatus=OPEN
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt_token}}

###

### Filter by both company and status — Google OPEN listings only
GET http://localhost:8080/api/job-listings/search?companyId=1&listingStatus=OPEN
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt_token}}


### ============================================================
### STEP 5 — Apply to positions
### Applications link to a listing (one-to-one enforced) and
### optionally to a contact. Status lifecycle:
###   APPLIED → PHONE_SCREEN → INTERVIEW → OFFER / REJECTED / WITHDRAWN
### ============================================================

### Apply to Google Backend Developer — referred by John Smith (with contact)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/applications
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt_token}}

{
  "dateApplied": "2026-02-15",
  "notes": "Referred by John Smith, the engineering manager",
  "applicationStatus": "APPLIED",
  "jobListingId": 1,
  "contactId": 1
}

###

### Apply to Microsoft Java Developer — found on LinkedIn (no contact yet)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/applications
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt_token}}

{
  "dateApplied": "2026-02-20",
  "notes": "Applied through LinkedIn",
  "applicationStatus": "APPLIED",
  "jobListingId": 3
}

###

### View all active applications
GET http://localhost:8080/api/applications
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt_token}}


### ============================================================
### STEP 6 — Progress the Google application through the lifecycle
### PATCH /status updates just the status field without requiring
### a full request body, keeping updates lightweight
### ============================================================

### Google app moves to phone screen
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/applications/1/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt_token}}

"PHONE_SCREEN"

###

### Phone screen went well — advance to interview
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/applications/1/status
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt_token}}

"INTERVIEW"

###

### Verify the status progression on the Google application
GET http://localhost:8080/api/applications/1
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt_token}}


### ============================================================
### STEP 7 — Update the Microsoft application with a full PUT
### Recruiter Jane reached out — link her as the contact and
### update the notes to reflect the new context
### ============================================================

PUT http://localhost:8080/api/applications/2
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt_token}}

{
  "dateApplied": "2026-02-20",
  "notes": "Recruiter Jane Doe reached out after LinkedIn application",
  "applicationStatus": "PHONE_SCREEN",
  "jobListingId": 3,
  "contactId": 2
}

###

### Verify the Microsoft application now has a contact linked
GET http://localhost:8080/api/applications/2
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt_token}}


### ============================================================
### STEP 8 — Cascade delete demonstration
### Deleting a company cascades to its listings and contacts.
### The Google application (id: 1) will also be removed since
### its listing is owned by Google.
### ============================================================

### Delete Microsoft (company id: 2)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/companies/2
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt_token}}

###

### Confirm Microsoft's listing is gone (expect 404)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/job-listings/3
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt_token}}

###

### Confirm only the Google application remains
GET http://localhost:8080/api/applications
Authorization: Bearer {{jwt_token}}
